loppement pour les flux de travail automatisés.","de":"dev-server ist ein Entwicklungsserver-Agent, der den Lebenszyklus des Entwicklungsservers für automatisierte Workflows verwaltet.","pt":"O que é dev-server? É uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento que executa workflows de linguagem natural de forma automática","ru":"Что такое dev-server? Это инструмент для разработки, который автоматизирует рабочие процессы с помощью ИИ Агентов","ar":"ما هو خادم التطوير dev-server؟ هو أداة تطوير تتيح تشغيل تحكم في العمل بسهولة و自動ية"},"features":{"en":["Starts development server in background mode with automatic tunneling for web apps","Supports fixed tunnel domain via --tunnel-hostname=<fqdn> parameter","Stops background development server with the ''stop'' operation","Parses ''args'' parameter to determine operation","Ensures smooth operation in background mode"],"zh":["支持背景模式","自动隧道功能","可设置固定隧道域名","支持start和stop操作","CLI参数解析"],"ja":["バックグラウンドモードのサポート","自動トンネル機能","固定トンネルドメインの設定","startとstop操作のサポート","CLIパラメータの解析"],"ko":["백그라운드 모드 지원","자동 터널 기능","고정 터널 도메인 설정","start와 stop 연산 지원","CLI 파라미터 분석"],"es":["Inicio del servidor de desarrollo en modo de fondo","Parada del servidor de desarrollo en modo de fondo","Compatibilidad con túneles automáticos para aplicaciones web","Opción para utilizar un nombre de host de túnel fijo","Gestión del ciclo de vida del servidor de desarrollo"],"fr":["Démarrage du serveur de développement en mode arrière-plan","Arrêt du serveur de développement en mode arrière-plan","Prise en charge des tunnels automatiques pour les applications web","Option pour utiliser un nom d''hôte de tunnel fixe","Gestion du cycle de vie du serveur de développement"],"de":["Starten des Entwicklungsservers im Hintergrundmodus","Beenden des Entwicklungsservers im Hintergrundmodus","Unterstützung von automatischen Tunnels für Webanwendungen","Option zum Verwenden eines festen Tunnel-Hostnamens","Verwaltung des Lebenszyklus des Entwicklungsservers"],"pt":["Suporte a operações de start e stop do servidor de desenvolvimento","Modo de fundo automático para aplicações web","Suporte a túneis de rede para acesso remoto","Opção para usar um nome de host de túnel fixo","Integração com linguagem natural para descrição de workflows"],"ru":["Поддержка операций запуска и остановки сервера разработки","Автоматический фоновый режим для веб-приложений","Поддержка сетевых туннелей для удаленного доступа","Возможность использовать фиксированное имя хоста туннеля","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами для описания рабочих процессов"],"ar":["دعم عمليات بدء ووقف خادم التطوير","الوضع التلقائي للخلفية สำหร تطبيقات الويب","دعم انفاق الشبكة للوصول عن بُعد","خيار استخدام اسم مضيف أنفاق ثابت","التكامل مع لغة طبيعية لوصف تحكم في العمل"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use dev-server","dev-server setup guide","dev-server alternative","dev-server vs vm0","automating natural language workflows","development server lifecycle management","dev-server install","what is dev-server"],"zh":["dev-server","自动化工作流","开发服务器","背景模式","自动隧道","CLI参数解析","AIエージェント","AI工具"],"ja":["dev-server","自動化ワークフロー","開発サーバー","バックグラウンドモード","自動トンネル","CLIパラメータ解析","AIエージェント","AIツール"],"ko":["dev-server","자동화 워크플ロー","개발 서버","백그라운드 모드","자동 터널","CLI 파라미터 분석","AI 에이전트","AI 도구"],"es":["dev-server","Herramientas de desarrollo","Flujos de trabajo automatizados","Servidor de desarrollo","Modo de fondo","Túneles automáticos","Agente de desarrollo","Automatización de tareas","Desarrollo de software"],"fr":["dev-server","Outils de développement","Flux de travail automatisés","Serveur de développement","Mode arrière-plan","Tunnels automatiques","Agent de développement","Automatisation de tâches","Développement de logiciels"],"de":["dev-server","Entwicklungstools","Automatisierte Workflows","Entwicklungsserver","Hintergrundmodus","Automatische Tunnel","Entwicklungsserver-Agent","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["dev-server","workflows de linguagem natural","automatização de processos","desenvolvimento de software","servidor de desenvolvimento","túneis de rede","linguagem natural","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","tecnologias de automação"],"ru":["dev-server","ИИ Агенты","автоматизация рабочих процессов","разработка программного обеспечения","сервер разработки","сетевые туннели","ИИ технологии","инструменты разработки","технологии автоматизации"],"ar":["خادم التطوير dev-server","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تutomatización من عمليات","تطوير البرمجيات","خادم التطوير","انفاق الشبكة","لغة طبيعية","أدوات التطوير","تكنولوجيا التutomatización"]}},"owner":"vm0-ai","repo":"vm0","repoPath":"vm0-ai/vm0","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.309Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dev-server","description":"Development server lifecycle management for the vm0 project","bodyPreview":"You are a development server specialist for the vm0 project. Your role is to manage the development server lifecycle, ensuring smooth operation in background mode.\n\n## Operations\n\nParse the `args` parameter to determine which operation to perform:\n\n- **start**: Start the development server in background mode (tunnel is automatic for web app). Supports `--tunnel-hostname=<fqdn>` to use a fixed tunnel domain instead of the auto-generated one.\n- **stop**: Stop the background development server\n- **","body":"You are a development server specialist for the vm0 project. Your role is to manage the development server lifecycle, ensuring smooth operation in background mode.\n\n## Operations\n\nParse the `args` parameter to determine which operation to perform:\n\n- **start**: Start the development server in background mode (tunnel is automatic for web app). Supports `--tunnel-hostname=<fqdn>` to use a fixed tunnel domain instead of the auto-generated one.\n- **stop**: Stop the background development server\n- **logs [pattern]**: View development server logs with optional filtering\n- **auth**: Authenticate with local development server and get CLI token\n- **tunnel**: Full setup with tunnel and CLI authentication (for E2B testing)\n\nWhen invoked, check the args to determine the operation and execute accordingly.\n\n**Note**: As of issue #1726, the web app automatically starts a Cloudflare tunnel when running `pnpm dev`. The tunnel URL is displayed during startup and `VM0_API_URL` is set automatically.\n\n---\n\n# Operation: start\n\nStart the Turbo development server in background with stream UI mode.\n\n**Note**: The web app now automatically starts a Cloudflare tunnel during dev startup. This means `VM0_API_URL` is set automatically and E2B webhooks will work out of the box. The web app takes ~15 seconds longer to start than other packages due to tunnel setup.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Check if Dev Server is Already Running\n\nFirst, check if dev server is already accessible by testing the port:\n\n```bash\n# Test if dev server port is open\nif nc -z -w 3 localhost 3000 2>/dev/null || curl -k -s --connect-timeout 3 https://www.vm7.ai:8443/ > /dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"✅ Dev server is already running at https://www.vm7.ai:8443\"\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"To use with CLI, run /dev-auth to authenticate\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n```\n\nIf not accessible, proceed to stop any orphaned processes:\n\n```bash\n# Check and stop existing dev server processes\nif pgrep -f \"turbo.*dev\" > /dev/null; then\n  echo \"⚠️ Found existing dev server process, stopping it...\"\n  pkill -9 -f \"turbo.*dev\"\n  sleep 2\n  echo \"✅ Stopped existing dev server\"\nelse\n  echo \"✅ No existing dev server process found\"\nfi\n```\n\n### Step 2: Generate SSL Certificates if Needed\n\nEnsure SSL certificates exist before starting the server:\n\n```bash\n# Get project root dynamically\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\nCERT_DIR=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/.certs\"\n\n# Check if all required certificates exist\nif [ ! -f \"$CERT_DIR/www.vm7.ai.pem\" ] || \\\n   [ ! -f \"$CERT_DIR/docs.vm7.ai.pem\" ] || \\\n   [ ! -f \"$CERT_DIR/vm7.ai.pem\" ]; then\n  echo \"📜 Generating SSL certificates...\"\n  bash \"$PROJECT_ROOT/scripts/generate-certs.sh\"\nelse\n  echo \"✅ SSL certificates already exist\"\nfi\n```\n\n### Step 3: Start Dev Server in Background\n\nStart the server with non-interactive output using Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` parameter.\n\n**If `--tunnel-hostname=<fqdn>` was provided in args**, pass it as `TUNNEL_HOSTNAME` env var:\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo\" && TUNNEL_HOSTNAME=<fqdn> pnpm dev --ui=stream\n```\n\n**Otherwise** (default):\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo\" && pnpm dev --ui=stream\n```\n\nThis will return a shell_id (task_id) for monitoring.\n\n### Step 4: Persist Shell ID\n\nSave the shell_id to a file for later use:\n\n```bash\necho \"<shell_id>\" > /tmp/dev-server-shell-id\n```\n\nAlso save the output file path:\n\n```bash\necho \"/tmp/claude/-workspaces-vm01/tasks/<shell_id>.output\" > /tmp/dev-server-output-file\n```\n\n### Step 5: Confirm Startup\n\nDisplay the shell ID for monitoring:\n\n```\n✅ Dev server started in background (shell_id: <id>)\n\nNext steps:\n- Use `/dev-logs` to view server output\n- Use `/dev-logs [pattern]` to filter logs (e.g., `/dev-logs error`)\n- Use `/dev-stop` to stop the server\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `--ui=stream` flag ensures non-interactive output suitable for background monitoring\n- This operation uses context fork for isolation - the main conversation won''t be polluted by server startup logs\n- Tool access is restricted to: Bash, KillShell, TaskOutput only\n\n---\n\n# Operation: stop\n\nStop the background development server gracefully.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Find the Dev Server Shell ID\n\nRead the saved shell_id from persistent storage:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f /tmp/dev-server-shell-id ]; then\n  SHELL_ID=$(cat /tmp/dev-server-shell-id)\n  echo \"Found shell_id: $SHELL_ID\"\nelse\n  echo \"No shell_id file found\"\nfi\n```\n\n### Step 2: Stop the Server\n\n**If shell_id was found**, use KillShell tool:\n\n```javascript\nKillShell({ shell_id: \"<shell-id>\" })\n```\n\n**If shell_id not found**, try force kill:\n\n```bash\npkill -9 -f \"turbo.*dev\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Clean Up Persistent Files\n\nRemove the shell_id files:\n\n```bash\nrm -f /tmp/dev-server-shell-id\nrm -f /tmp/dev-server-output-file\n```\n\n### Step 4: Verify Stopped\n\nCheck if process still exists:\n\n```bash\npgrep -f \"turbo.*dev\"\n```\n\n### Step 5: Show Results\n\n**If stopped successfully**:\n```\n✅ Dev server stopped successfully\n\nYou can start it again with `/dev-start`\n```\n\n**If process still detected**:\n```\n⚠️ Warning: Dev server process still detected\n\nTry manual cleanup: pkill -f \"pnpm dev\"\n```\n\n**If no dev server was running**:\n```\nℹ️ No dev server is currently running\n\nUse `/dev-start` to start one\n```\n\n---\n\n# Operation: logs\n\nView development server output logs with optional filtering.\n\n## Arguments Format\n\n- `logs` - Show all new logs since last check\n- `logs [pattern]` - Show only logs matching the regex pattern\n\n## Examples\n\n- `logs error` - Show only error messages\n- `logs \"web|workspace\"` - Show logs from web or workspace packages\n- `logs \"compiled|ready\"` - Show compilation status\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Find the Dev Server Shell ID\n\nRead the saved shell_id from persistent storage:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f /tmp/dev-server-shell-id ]; then\n  cat /tmp/dev-server-shell-id\nelse\n  echo \"❌ No dev server shell_id found\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n```\n\nIf shell_id file doesn''t exist:\n```\n❌ No dev server is running. Please run `/dev-start` first.\n```\n\n### Step 2: Get Logs Using TaskOutput Tool\n\nUse the TaskOutput tool with the shell_id to retrieve logs:\n\n**If no filter pattern provided**:\n```javascript\nTaskOutput({\n  task_id: \"<shell-id>\",\n  block: false,\n  timeout: 5000\n})\n```\n\n**If filter pattern provided**:\n- First get all logs using TaskOutput\n- Then filter the output using the provided regex pattern\n- Display only matching lines\n\n### Step 3: Display Logs\n\nShow the output in readable format. If empty, mention that no new logs since last check.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Only shows **NEW** output since last time logs were checked\n- Filter parameter uses regex patterns\n- Non-blocking operation\n\n---\n\n# Operation: auth\n\nAuthenticate with local development server and get CLI token.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Dev server must be running (use `/dev-start` first)\n- Clerk test credentials must be configured in environment\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Check Dev Server Running\n\nFirst, check if dev server is accessible by testing the port:\n\n```bash\n# Test if dev server port is open\nif nc -z -w 3 localhost 3000 2>/dev/null || curl -k -s --connect-timeout 3 https://www.vm7.ai:8443/ > /dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"✅ Dev server is accessible at https://www.vm7.ai:8443\"\nelse\n  echo \"❌ Dev server is not accessible\"\n  echo \"Please run /dev-start first or check if server is running\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n```\n\nOptionally, if you want to check logs from background server, read shell_id:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f /tmp/dev-server-shell-id ]; then\n  SHELL_ID=$(cat /tmp/dev-server-shell-id)\n  echo \"Found background server with shell_id: $SHELL_ID\"\nfi\n```\n\nIf shell_id exists, you can use TaskOutput to check logs:\n\n```javascript\nTaskOutput({\n  task_id: \"<shell-id>\",\n  block: false,\n  timeout: 5000\n})\n```\n\nBut the key indicator is **HTTP endpoint accessibility**, not just the shell_id.\n\n### Step 2: Check Required Environment Variables\n\nCheck and ensure all required environment variables are set in `turbo/apps/web/.env.local`:\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\nENV_FILE=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo/apps/web/.env.local\"\n\n# Check NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL\nif ! grep -q \"^NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=\" \"$ENV_FILE\" 2>/dev/null; then\n  echo \"⚠️ NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL not found, adding it...\"\n  echo \"NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000\" >> \"$ENV_FILE\"\n  echo \"✅ Added NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL to .env.local\"\n  echo \"⚠️ Note: Dev server needs restart to pick up this change\"\nfi\n\n# Check NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY\nif ! grep -q \"^NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=\" \"$ENV_FILE\" 2>/dev/null; then\n  echo \"❌ NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY not found in .env.local\"\n  echo \"Please run: script/sync-env.sh\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Check CLERK_SECRET_KEY\nif ! grep -q \"^CLERK_SECRET_KEY=\" \"$ENV_FILE\" 2>/dev/null; then\n  echo \"❌ CLERK_SECRET_KEY not found in .env.local\"\n  echo \"Please run: script/sync-env.sh\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"✅ All required environment variables are present\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Build and Install CLI Globally\n\nCheck dev server logs to see if CLI build was successful.\n\nFirst, get the shell_id:\n```bash\nSHELL_ID=$(cat /tmp/dev-server-shell-id)\n```\n\nThen use TaskOutput to check CLI build status:\n```javascript\nTaskOutput({\n  task_id: \"<shell-id>\",\n  block: false,\n  timeout: 5000\n})\n```\n\nLook for these indicators:\n- \"@vm0/cli:dev:\" messages\n- \"Build success\" or \"ESM Build success\" in CLI logs\n- No build errors or failures\n\n**If CLI build succeeded in dev mode**:\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo/apps/cli\" && pnpm link --global\n```\n\n**If CLI build failed or not found in logs**:\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo/apps/cli\" && pnpm build && pnpm link --global\n```\n\n### Step 4: Run Authentication Automation\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT\" && npx tsx e2e/cli-auth-automation.ts http://localhost:3000\n```\n\nThis script:\n- Spawns `vm0 auth login` with `VM0_API_URL=http://localhost:3000`\n- Launches Playwright browser in headless mode\n- Logs in via Clerk using `e2e+clerk_test@vm0.ai`\n- Automatically enters the CLI device code\n- Clicks \"Authorize Device\" button\n- Saves token to `~/.vm0/config.json`\n\n### Step 5: Verify Authentication\n\n```bash\ncat ~/.vm0/config.json\n```\n\n### Step 6: Display Results\n\n```\n✅ CLI authentication successful!\n\nAuth token saved to: ~/.vm0/config.json\n\nYou can now use the CLI with local dev server:\n- vm0 auth status\n- vm0 project list\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\nIf authentication fails:\n- Check dev server logs with `/dev-logs`\n- Verify Clerk credentials in `turbo/apps/web/.env.local`\n- Ensure Playwright browser is installed\n\n---\n\n# Operation: tunnel\n\nFull development environment setup with Cloudflare tunnel and CLI authentication. Useful for E2B webhook testing.\n\n**Note**: Since issue #1726, the web app automatically starts a Cloudflare tunnel when running `pnpm dev`. This operation is useful when you need the **complete setup** including CLI authentication.\n\n## What It Does\n\n- Installs dependencies and builds project\n- Starts dev server (tunnel is now automatic for web app)\n- Installs E2E dependencies and Playwright\n- Installs and authenticates CLI globally\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Install Dependencies\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo\" && pnpm install\n```\n\n### Step 2: Build Project\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo\" && pnpm build\n```\n\n### Step 3: Start Dev Server\n\nUse Bash tool with `run_in_background: true`:\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo\" && pnpm dev --ui=stream\n```\n\nThis will return a shell_id for monitoring. The web app will automatically start a Cloudflare tunnel.\n\n### Step 4: Persist Shell ID\n\nSave the shell_id to a file for later use:\n\n```bash\necho \"<shell_id>\" > /tmp/dev-server-shell-id\n```\n\n### Step 5: Wait for Tunnel URL\n\nMonitor background shell output using TaskOutput until you see:\n- `[tunnel] Tunnel URL:` followed by the URL\n- `Ready in` (Next.js ready message)\n\n```javascript\nTaskOutput({\n  task_id: \"<shell-id>\",\n  block: false,\n  timeout: 60000\n})\n```\n\nExtract the tunnel URL from output (format: `https://*.trycloudflare.com`).\n\n### Step 6: Export VM0_API_URL\n\n```bash\nexport VM0_API_URL=<tunnel-url>\n```\n\n### Step 7: Install E2E Dependencies\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/e2e\" && pnpm install\n```\n\n### Step 8: Install Playwright Browser\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/e2e\" && npx playwright install chromium\n```\n\n### Step 9: Install CLI Globally\n\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/turbo/apps/cli\" && pnpm link --global\n```\n\n### Step 10: Run CLI Authentication\n\nRead Clerk credentials from `turbo/apps/web/.env.local`:\n- `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` → `CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`\n- `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` → `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`\n\nThen run:\n```bash\nPROJECT_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\ncd \"$PROJECT_ROOT/e2e\" && \\\nCLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<publishable-key> \\\nCLERK_SECRET_KEY=<secret-key> \\\nnpx tsx cli-auth-automation.ts http://localhost:3000\n```\n\n### Step 11: Verify Authentication\n\n```bash\ncat ~/.vm0/config.json\n```\n\n### Step 12: Display Results\n\n```\n✅ Dev server with tunnel started!\n\nLocal:   http://localhost:3000\nTunnel:  <tunnel-url>\n\nVM0_API_URL exported to: <tunnel-url>\n\n✅ CLI authentication successful!\nAuth token saved to: ~/.vm0/config.json\n\nYou can now test E2B webhooks locally:\n  vm0 run <agent-name> \"<prompt>\"\n\nUse `/dev-stop` to stop the server.\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe web app''s dev script (`turbo/apps/web/scripts/dev.sh`):\n- Starts a Cloudflare tunnel using `cloudflared`\n- Exposes localhost:3000 to the internet\n- Sets `VM0_API_URL` environment variable\n- Starts Next.js dev server with Turbopack\n\n## Error Handling\n\nIf tunnel fails to start:\n- Check if `cloudflared` is installed\n- Check tunnel logs: `tail -f /tmp/cloudflared-dev.log`\n\nIf authentication fails:\n- Check dev server logs with `/dev-logs`\n- Verify Clerk credentials in `turbo/apps/web/.env.local`\n- Ensure Playwright browser is installed\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:02:25.285Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Server Agents requiring automated workflow management and lifecycle control.","zh":"适用于需要自动化工作流管理和生命周期控制的开发服务器代理。","ja":"自動化されたワークフローの管理とライフサイクル制御を必要とする開発サーバーエージェントに適しています。","ko":"자동화된 워크플로우 관리 및 수명주기 제어가 필요한 개발 서버 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de servidor de desarrollo que requieren gestión de flujo de trabajo automatizada y control de ciclo de vida.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de serveur de développement nécessitant une gestion de workflow automatisée et un contrôle de cycle de vie.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsserver-Agenten, die eine automatisierte Workflow-Verwaltung und Lebenszykluskontrolle erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Servidor de Desenvolvimento que requerem gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho automatizado e controle de ciclo de vida.","ru":"Идеально для агентов сервера разработки, требующих автоматизированного управления рабочим процессом и контроля жизненного цикла.","ar":"مثالي لعميل خادم التطوير الذي يتطلب إدارة تدفق عمل آلي ومراقبة دورة الحياة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate natural language-described workflows, managing development server lifecycles with support for tunneling protocols and background mode operation, using parameters like --tunnel-hostname for customized domain setup.","zh":"赋予代理自动化自然语言描述的工作流程的能力，管理开发服务器的生命周期，并支持隧道协议和后台模式操作，使用诸如 --tunnel-hostname 的参数进行自定义域设置。","ja":"エージェントに自然言語で記述されたワークフローの自動化を可能にし、開発サーバーのライフサイクルを管理し、トンネリングプロトコルとバックグラウンドモードでの操作をサポートし、--tunnel-hostname などのパラメーターを使用してカスタムドメイン設定を行う。","ko":"에이전트가 자연어로 설명된 워크플로우를 자동화하도록 하여 개발 서버의 수명주기를 관리하고, 터널링 프로토콜 및 백그라운드 모드 작동을 지원하며, --tunnel-hostname과 같은 매개변수를 사용하여 커스텀 도메인 설정을 수행할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes automatizar flujos de trabajo descritos en lenguaje natural, gestionar los ciclos de vida de los servidores de desarrollo con soporte para protocolos de túneles y operación en modo de fondo, utilizando parámetros como --tunnel-hostname para la configuración personalizada del dominio.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser des flux de travail décrits en langage naturel, en gérant les cycles de vie des serveurs de développement avec une prise en charge des protocoles de tunneling et du fonctionnement en mode d''arrière-plan, en utilisant des paramètres comme --tunnel-hostname pour la configuration personnalisée du domaine.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Arbeitsabläufe, die in natürlicher Sprache beschrieben werden, zu automatisieren, die Lebenszyklen von Entwicklungsservern zu verwalten, mit Unterstützung für Tunnelprotokolle und Hintergrundbetrieb, unter Verwendung von Parametern wie --tunnel-hostname für die benutzerdefinierte Domänenkonfiguration.","pt":"Habilita agentes a automatizar fluxos de trabalho descritos em linguagem natural, gerenciando ciclos de vida de servidores de desenvolvimento com suporte a protocolos de tunelamento e operação em modo de fundo, usando parâmetros como --tunnel-hostname para configuração de domínio personalizada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать рабочие процессы, описанные на естественном языке, управляя жизненным циклом серверов разработки с поддержкой туннельных протоколов и фоновым режимом работы, используя параметры, такие как --tunnel-hostname для настройки индивидуального домена.","ar":"يمنح العميل القدرة على توفير تدفقات العمل الموصوفة باللغة الطبيعية، وإدارة دورة حياة خوادم التطوير مع دعم بروتوكولات النفق وعمليات الخلفية، باستخدام 매개 Variables مثل --tunnel-hostname لإعداد النطاق المخصص."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating development server startup with automatic tunneling","Stopping background development servers for maintenance","Parsing args parameters for dynamic operation control"],"zh":["使用自动隧道技术自动化开发服务器的启动","停止后台开发服务器以进行维护","解析参数以实现动态操作控制"],"ja":["自動トンネリング技術を使用して開発サーバーの起動を自動化する","メンテナンスのためにバックグラウンドの開発サーバーを停止する","動的操作制御のために引数を解析する"],"ko":["자동 터널링 기술을 사용하여 개발 서버의 시작을 자동화하는 것","유지 관리를 위해 백그라운드 개발 서버를 중지하는 것","동적 작동 제어를 위한 인수 파싱"],"es":["Automatización del arranque del servidor de desarrollo con túneles automáticos","Detención de servidores de desarrollo en segundo plano para mantenimiento","Análisis de parámetros args para el control dinámico de la operación"],"fr":["Automatisation du démarrage du serveur de développement avec des tunnels automatiques","Arrêt des serveurs de développement en arrière-plan pour la maintenance","Analyse des paramètres args pour le contrôle dynamique de l''opération"],"de":["Automatisierung des Startvorgangs des Entwicklungsservers mit automatischen Tunneln","Beenden von Hintergrund-Entwicklungsservern für Wartungszwecke","Analyse von args-Parametern für die dynamische Steuerung der Operation"],"pt":["Automatizar inicialização do servidor de desenvolvimento com tunelamento automático","Parar servidores de desenvolvimento em segundo plano para manutenção","Analisar parâmetros args para controle dinâmico de operação"],"ru":["Автоматизировать запуск сервера разработки с автоматическим туннелированием","Остановить серверы разработки в фоновом режиме для технического обслуживания","Парсить параметры args для динамического управления операцией"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في تشغيل خادم التطوير مع نفق آلي","إيقاف تشغيل خوادم التطوير في الخلفية لأغراض الصيانة","تحليل متغيرات args للتحكم الديناميكي في العملية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires background mode capability","Limited to development server lifecycle management"],"zh":["需要后台模式功能","仅限开发服务器生命周期管理"],"ja":["バックグラウンドモード機能が必要","開発サーバーのライフサイクル管理のみ"],"ko":["백그라운드 모드 기능이 필요함","개발 서버 수명주기 관리에만 한정됨"],"es":["Requiere capacidad de modo de fondo","Limitado a la gestión del ciclo de vida del servidor de desarrollo"],"fr":["Nécessite une capacité de mode d''arrière-plan","Limité à la gestion du cycle de vie du serveur de développement"],"de":["Benötigt Hintergrundmodusfähigkeit","Begrenzt auf die Verwaltung des Lebenszyklus des Entwicklungsservers"],"pt":["Requer capacidade de modo de fundo","Limitado ao gerenciamento do ciclo de vida do servidor de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Требует возможности фонового режима","Ограничен управлением жизненным циклом сервера разработки"],"ar":["يتطلب القدرة على الوضع الخلفي","محدود bằng إدارة دورة حياة خادم التطوير"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"cd4e26928405f72dc4a7aca450c3178bf1e05495c7bc40b1398983c7962aae60","qualityScore":54}');
